    {
     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Language focus",
     "title": "It shows · it measures: the -s",
     "steps": [
      [
       "it / he / she",
       "The radar show<b>s</b> ships."
      ],
      [
       "question",
       "What <b>does</b> it do?"
      ],
      [
       "answer",
       "It measure<b>s</b> the depth."
      ]
     ],
     "paras": [
      "To say what something does (always, every day), use the simple verb. With <b>it, he, she</b> add <b>-s</b>.",
      "In the question, <b>does</b> carries the -s, so the verb has none: <i>What does it <b>do</b>?</i>"
     ],
     "avoid": "The radar show ships. · What it does? · What does it shows?"
    },
    {
     "type": "choice",
     "q": "The ECDIS ___ our position.",
     "opts": [
      "shows",
      "show",
      "showing"
     ],
     "a": 0
    },
    {
     "type": "choice",
     "q": "Which question is correct?",
     "opts": [
      "What does the gyro compass do?",
      "What does the gyro compass does?",
      "What the gyro compass does?"
     ],
     "a": 0
    },
    {
     "type": "build",
     "situation": "Diego asks about the echo sounder.",
     "q": "Answer him.",
     "a": [
